's value has been artificially held  up you don't get a discount because it's  manipulated russia has since removed  some restrictions on selling rubles and  the central bank has cut its rates that  is reducing some of the pain for russian  citizens from the sanctions and cutting  back on the expected economic impact of  the war researchers at jp morgan had  expected russia's economy to contract by  35 percent in the second quarter after  sanctions were imposed in march but the  bank now predicts it will shrink by only  about one-fourth of that that recovery  was boosted by increased oil sales to  europe and asia and a stronger currency  keeping a lid on inflation the improved  economic situation provides some cover  for putin and the russian government to  continue the assault on ukraine the big  picture for the rest of the world is the  longer russia is at war with ukraine the  longer we see shortages and delays for  products like wheat and oil that's  pushing up inflation and adding to  supply chain disruptions  this could mean more high prices for  food gas utilities and much more  it's a tough world out there as hip-hop  billionaire jay-z reminds us he says my  mind on my money money on my mind if you  owe me ten dollars you ain't giving me  nine  that's all for now i'll see you next  time
 

